{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-215509",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-x|-8 & =7 \\\\ |5-x| & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|5-x|=5-x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-x| & =15 \\\\ 5-x & =15 \\\\ -x & =10 \\\\ x & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|5-x|=-(5-x),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-x| & =15 \\\\ -(5-x) & =15 \\\\ -5+x & =15 \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-10$ and $x=20.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
